Monsters prefer artifacts above all other weapons (even the +0 Sting
above a +5 dwarvish mattock), but aligned artifacts can only be used by
monsters of the correct alignment. You have Cleaver and Vorpal Blade
which are neutral and so can only be used by neutral pets, which are
quite rare (weapon-wielding ones that is). Iron golems are neutral and
can wield weapons, but are instakilled by rust traps and cannot use
unicorn horns. If I even gave Vorpal Blade to a pet, that pet would have
to possess a unicorn horn, to prevent me from being beheaded by a
confused pet.

If no artifact is available, just the weapon type matters. The preferred
weapon type then is a cocktrice corpse, and yes, monsters can be stoned
too if they fall into a pit while wielding one.

You can remove a weapon from a pet by applying a bullwhip. You need at
least 15 dexterity if you are not an archeologist. Assuming you are not
confused, fumbling, etc., this does not anger or harm the pet in any
way.

